          "question": "What is the difference between E11 and E11.9, and when is each the right thing to quote?",
          "answer": "E11 and E11.9 are codes from the ICD-10 classification system used to denote diabetes mellitus type 2. \n\nE11 refers to \"Type 2 diabetes mellitus.\" It is a broad code that encompasses all presentations of type 2 diabetes.\n\nE11.9 specifies \"Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications.\" This code is used when documenting cases of type 2 diabetes that do not involve any complications such as neuropathy, retinopathy, or cardiovascular issues.\n\nIn summary, use E11 for general cases of type 2 diabetes and E11.9 when there are no complications present.\n\nI could not cover more specific details about managing diabetes or other related codes.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
